    {
        _plaDeferPullOne = false;
        _visiblePC = _opcodeAddress;           // stay on opcode
        _cycle = 2 // force one more tick so we hit cycle 1 again for the real pull
        return;                                 // don't execute yet
    }
    // normal path (non-defer)
    FinishStagedMemoryRead();  // A and S updated
    _cycle = 0;                // fall through to apply 0x68
    break;
```

Then in the deferred case, after the pull actually happens on the next tick, you still need to suppress the boundary so the PC getter returns _visiblePC instead of _pc (which is already EB19).

